## Investigation evidence (moved out of the description per P4)

### 1. setup-uv v10.0.0 resolution path, read at the pinned SHA

Source obtained from `https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/setup-uv/tarball/ae62891fec2bb8e7d6c99fc78c9fec3a63790f8d` — the exact SHA every call site pins.

`src/version/version-request-resolver.ts`, resolver order:

    const VERSION_REQUEST_RESOLVERS: VersionRequestResolver[] = [
      new ExplicitInputVersionResolver(),   // the `version:` input
      new VersionFileVersionResolver(),     // the `version-file:` input
      new WorkspaceVersionResolver(),       // uv.toml, then pyproject.toml
      new LatestVersionResolver(),          // "latest"
    ];

`WorkspaceVersionResolver` scans exactly two paths and emits the observed log line on miss:

    getWorkspaceCandidates() {
      return [
        { source: "uv.toml",        sourcePath: path.join(this.workingDirectory, "uv.toml") },
        { source: "pyproject.toml", sourcePath: path.join(this.workingDirectory, "pyproject.toml") },
      ];
    }
    ...
    log.info("Could not determine uv version from uv.toml or pyproject.toml. Falling back to latest.");

Note that `ExplicitInputVersionResolver` runs BEFORE the workspace scan — that is precisely why a
per-call-site `version:` input would silently override the single source, and why the guard forbids one.

`src/version/resolve.ts`, concrete resolution — exact is first and returns without touching the network:

    const CONCRETE_VERSION_RESOLVERS: ConcreteVersionResolver[] = [
      new ExactVersionResolver(),   // returns parsedSpecifier.normalized immediately
      new LatestVersionResolver(),  // await getLatestVersion(manifestUrl)   <-- the fetch
      new RangeVersionResolver(),   // await getAllVersions(manifestUrl)     <-- also a fetch
    ];

`src/version/specifier.ts` — why the `==` form matters:

    export function normalizeVersionSpecifier(specifier: string): string {
      const trimmedSpecifier = specifier.trim();
      if (trimmedSpecifier.startsWith("==")) { return trimmedSpecifier.slice(2); }
      return trimmedSpecifier;
    }
    ...
    if (tc.isExplicitVersion(normalized)) { return { kind: "exact", normalized, raw }; }
    return { isSimpleMinimumVersionSpecifier: raw.includes(">") && !raw.includes(","), kind: "range", ... };

So `"==0.12.7"` -> `"0.12.7"` -> `kind: "exact"` -> no network. `">=0.12.7"` -> `kind: "range"` -> still fetches.

`src/version/file-parser.ts` — the pyproject key that is read:

    const requiredVersion = pyproject.tool?.uv?.["required-version"];
    if (requiredVersion !== undefined) { return requiredVersion; }
    return getUvVersionFromParsedPyproject(pyproject);   // fallback: a `uv<spec>` dependency

### 2. Call-site census

`grep -rn "setup-uv@" .github/workflows/` -> 25 sites in 12 files:
_build-and-test.yml:63,264,423; _eval-discipline.yml:59; _mutation.yml:56,121;
dependency-advisory-canary.yml:85; external-integration.yml:111,273,431,538,668,818,932;
gerrit-verify.yaml:178; jira-dc-capability-map.yml:39; jira-dc-richtext-probe.yml:40;
prompt-eval.yml:68; release.yml:107; structured-output-baseline.yml:56;
test.yml:105,303,341,369,402.

None sets `working-directory` (the action defaults it to `${{ github.workspace }}`), so all 25 resolve
against the repository root. A backwards scan to the job boundary found a checkout preceding each one:
24 via `actions/checkout@...`, and `gerrit-verify.yaml:178` via
`lfreleng-actions/checkout-gerrit-change-action@f87b90a3...` at line 170. So `pyproject.toml` is on disk
before setup-uv runs at every site — the precondition the chosen mechanism depends on.

### 3. Version-in-force evidence (run 33225196631, 2026-08-29)

    build-and-test / lint + type-check  01:08:42Z  Could not determine uv version from uv.toml or pyproject.toml. Falling back to latest.
    build-and-test / lint + type-check  01:08:42Z  Fetching manifest data from https://raw.githubusercontent.com/astral-sh/versions/main/v1/uv.ndjson ...
    build-and-test / lint + type-check  01:08:42Z  Downloading uv from "https://releases.astral.sh/github/uv/releases/download/0.12.7/uv-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz" ...
    build-and-test / lint + type-check  01:08:43Z  Successfully installed uv version 0.12.7

Same 0.12.7 in `sweep (py3.14)`, `sweep (py3.15)`, `sweep (py3.14t)` and `sweep (macos, full suite)` of the
same run. PyPI currently reports uv 0.12.7 as latest, consistent with "falling back to latest" resolving there.
Pinning 0.12.7 is therefore behaviour-preserving for CI.

### 4. uv's own enforcement of required-version (local probe, uv 0.7.18)

Scratch `pyproject.toml` with `[tool.uv] required-version = "==0.12.7"`, then `uv pip list`:

    error: Required uv version `==0.12.7` does not match the running version `0.7.18`.
    Update `uv` by running `uv self update 0.12.7`.

Confirms the accepted consequence recorded in the plan, and that the remedy is a single self-describing command.
